{"id": "EUVD-2026-108185", "enisaUuid": "49701881-ce6f-3d5b-9188-a0aa9c51b711", "description": "In EmberZNet 9.1.1 and earlier, a malformed Simple_Desc_req response can result in an out-of-bounds write potentially leading to remote code execution. This response must come from a device that has already joined the network, and the attacker must wait for a Simple_Desc_req before the attack can be performed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T13:46:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:00:32", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/SiliconLabsSoftware/docs-security-advisories/blob/main/Advisories/500-599/A-00000589.md"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-85079", "GHSA-4crr-j758-m3h5"], "assigner": "Silabs", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "68609961-d9ab-3b9d-9bcd-23e095430a60", "product": {"name": "EmberZNet", "vendor": {"name": "silabs.com"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c6fd327a-a156-300e-aa1b-0f86df8009fc", "vendor": {"name": "Silicon Labs"}}], "isExploited": false}